{
  "article": {
    "introduction": "She is the psychic daughter of one of Europe's longest-reigning monarchs; he is a self-proclaimed sixth-generation shaman from California. The wedding of Princess Märtha Louise of Norway to Durek Verrett on Saturday afternoon was far from a typical royal ceremony, yet it attracted onlookers lining the cloudy streets of Geiranger, eager to see the bride.",
    "background": "At 52 years old, Märtha Louise is the only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, and she ranks fourth in line for the Norwegian throne. She wed Verrett, 49, in a traditional ceremony held at a church in Norway, attended by a mix of royalty and celebrities at the four-star Hotel Union in a small village by the Geiranger fjord.",
    "details": "Accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her first marriage to the late Norwegian author Ari Behn, whom she divorced in 2017, the princess had a guest list of 350. Notable attendees included her brother, Crown Prince Haakon and his wife, Crown Princess Mette-Marit; Sweden's Crown Princess Victoria and her husband, Prince Daniel; and Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands.",
    "personal_history": "Princess Märtha Louise has led an unconventional royal lifestyle, having publicly identified as a clairvoyant and managing a healing school for a decade where she taught people how to connect with angels. In 2022, she announced her intention to step back from official royal responsibilities to concentrate on her and Verrett's business and to clearly separate their endeavors from the Norwegian royal family.",
    "verrett_description": "Verrett refers to himself on Instagram as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator', and he has worked with notable clients including Gwyneth Paltrow, whom he has referred to as a 'soul sister'."
  }
}
```

